{
  "about": "What every host that formats numbers and instants writes, for tests/expectations/mod.rs to run through the public Localizer: the ICU4X host of the daemon (tests/lanes/icu.rs) and, later, the browser's Intl. Made by generate.mjs from Node's Intl as an oracle. Differences from V8: en-US writes U+202F before AM and PM, as CLDR does, where V8 writes U+0020, so a host running on V8 folds U+202F and U+00A0 to U+0020 before comparing. A number literal's decimals are its minimum fraction digits, and the maximum wins over a larger minimum; a count above 2^53 is its digits. A size and a duration are the en-US catalog's helpers around numbers written by the locale. An instant with no zone, or a zone nobody has, is read as UTC. Sizes, counts and durations travel as text, which holds a 64-bit number exactly.",
